{
  "case_id": "2006-05-746",
  "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 12:59 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern Railway",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The fundamental question in this case is whether the common law doctrine of equivalence between defendant negligence and plaintiff negligence applies under the FELA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Except that the -- what was it, the Rogers case, which said that the -- well, you debate whether it said that, but let's assume that it said that the rule of proximate causality doesn't apply to the negligence of the defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I take it you would be satisfied -- not wholly satisfied, but substantially satisfied if we said, yeah, we accept the doctrine of equivalence, and we think the instruction on contributory negligence was correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But I thought you argued the Rogers standard was a correct standard in the Missouri court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: As we're supposed to decide the case, in your view, there was instruction 13. Instruction 13 used the word direct. MR. PHILLIPS: Yes. JUSTICE BREYER: You object to 13. You said it should use the word in whole or in part."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Phillips, may I ask you this question. Assuming you're right on the doctrine of equivalence and you're wrong on proximate cause, for the moment. Now, you said earlier in your argument, it is perfectly clear there was no harmless error here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, no, no. May I pick you up on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PERRY: And he, you know, definitely clearly said that a railroad worker does not have to prove common law proximate causation relying on Rogers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Can you have more than one proximate cause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-746",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8694558b226e3a5be206dd07a058401332b1c7f473dd48eb8b49c547ea9b8e89",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8694558b226e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
